<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Benchmark Specification and Evaluated Models</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Benchmark Task Coverage and Provenance</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">EdgeKernelBench contains 331 canonical tasks across three complexity levels. Level 1 comprises 128 <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Basic Compute Patterns</em>, Level 2 comprises 162 <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Composed Operator Graphs</em>, and Level 3 comprises 41 <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Compact Model Graphs</em>. We further organize the tasks into mobile and personal intelligence, embodied robotics, and smart AIoT applications. This application-based grouping accounts for the diversity of workloads and deployment requirements across fragmented edge platforms. Using this application-based organization, we instantiate evaluation tasks for the scenarios represented by each platform. The resulting evaluation sets contain 91/93/20 task instances on CPU/LLVM, 98/95/25 on GPU/CUDA, and 98/105/25 on GPU/OpenCL for Levels 1, 2, and 3, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The benchmark combines manually authored tasks with implementations rewritten and adapted from selected representative open-source libraries. For tasks derived from open-source libraries, we document the original source and the changes made during adaptation. Before inclusion, each task is normalized to a static, self-contained PyTorch interface and checked for importability, interface completeness, and consistent shape materialization.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.1 Benchmark Task Coverage and Provenance ‣ Appendix A Benchmark Specification and Evaluated Models ‣ EdgeKernelBench: Unified LLM-DrivenKernel Generation for Edge Backends" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes representative tasks at each complexity level.</p>
</div>
