<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Generation and evaluation run in isolated environments to prevent access to hidden evaluation data or interference with scoring.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Agent Prompt Protocols</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent optimization uses the same public reference and tensor specifications as direct generation, with iterative evaluation within the assigned budget. The templates below describe the optimization roles and their interaction with the evaluator.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">F.2.1 </span>Pure Claude Code Baseline Prompt</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pure Claude Code baseline uses the same base model, public task specification, evaluator, and wall-clock budget as LEKA. A persistent Claude Code session uses the task definition and its initial high-level IR to construct and refine complete candidates. The implementation-independent core prompt is summarized below.</p>
